    "notes": "1. Total Revenue is constructed as the sum of all revenue line items listed under 'Revenue' and 'Interest income' from the primary statement. This includes 'Noninterest revenue' components and 'Net interest income' components. 2. Total Operating Cost includes all costs that are part of the income generation process before arriving at 'Income before income tax expense'. This includes 'Interest expense', 'Provision for credit losses', and all components of 'Total noninterest expense'. 3. For a bank, 'Interest expense' is a core operating cost of funding its interest-earning assets and is included in total_operating_cost. It is also listed separately under interest_expenses. 4. 'Provision for credit losses' is a standard operating cost for a financial institution. 5. The sign convention for total_operating_cost, taxes, and interest_expenses follows Rule 13: items that reduce income (expenses) are positive. Therefore, all values for these fields are positive numbers as extracted, even though some source items (like 'Investment securities losses') are presented as negatives in the revenue section. 6. The 'scale' is 1,000,000 as the statement is in millions. 7. All supplementary tables provide detailed breakdowns but do not introduce new top-level line items for the consolidated income statement; they are used for verification and context.",
